   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "One direction or a visit",
     "texto": [
      "Идти (on foot) and ехать (by vehicle) describe movement in one direction: шёл/шла/шло/шли and ехал/ехала/ехало/ехали.",
      "Ходить and ездить describe round trips, visits or repeated and habitual movements. Ходить в кино can mean going to the cinema and does not, by itself, say how one got there; ездить expresses travel by vehicle."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Gender and number in the past",
     "texto": [
      "In the singular, the form agrees with masculine, feminine or neuter; in the plural the plural form is used. The table gathers the endings and the irregular forms of these verbs.",
      "Шёл/ехал usually present the trip in one direction as a process: шёл в кино = he was on his way to the cinema. Ходил/ездил can express a visit or a round trip, or a habit. The context decides; it is not enough to count whether it happened once."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
